# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will write a clear technical spec and build plan for your app idea
category: Programming & Tech
subcategory: Software Development
tags:
  - technical spec
  - architecture
  - mvp plan
  - requirements
  - roadmap
description: >-
  Have an app idea but no plan a developer (or an AI) can build from? I turn it into a clear spec:
  what it does, how it fits together, and the order to build it in.


  I work spec-first on my own large system: over a hundred build maps, each phase naming its files,
  what it depends on, and the test that proves it is done. That is how a big project stays
  buildable, and it is what you get.


  What you get:

  - The idea in plain words: who it is for and what "done" looks like

  - The parts of the system and how they talk to each other

  - A build plan in phases, smallest useful version first

  - For each phase: what to build, what it depends on, how to test it

  - Risks and failure points named up front


  Hand it to any developer or AI coding tool and they can start straight away.


  How it works: a short call or written brief, then a draft, then your feedback.
packages:
  basic:
    name: One-Page Brief
    description: 'Your idea as a one-page brief: goal, users, features, done-when.'
    deliveryDays: 2
    revisions: 1
    price: 50
    features: {}        # Fiverr's package rows for this subcategory, as the page labels them; the fill lists the rows it finds
  standard:
